From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:13:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] home: fill a window wider than 16:9

The dashboard sizes everything from the window's height and lays it
out in a 16:9 box. On the 1920x720 cluster output the box is 1280x720,
so the gauges sit in the middle with black bars at both sides.

When the window is wider than 16:9, keep its full width instead of
cutting it to the box. The sizes still follow the height; the rows
that place the gauges at both ends (spaceBetween) spread them over the
width.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/lib/screen/home.dart
+++ b/lib/screen/home.dart
@@ -99,9 +99,11 @@
     double ratHeight = (windowWidth * 9) / 16;
     double ratWidth = (windowHeight * 16) / 9;
 
+    // The sizes follow the height, so a window wider than 16:9 (the
+    // 1920x720 cluster) keeps its full width: the gauges move apart instead
+    // of leaving black bars at the sides.
     if (ratWidth <= windowWidth) {
       screenHeight = windowHeight;
-      screenWidth = ratWidth;
     } else {
       screenHeight = ratHeight;
       screenWidth = windowWidth;
